certain obligations.—A person is guilty of an offence punishable with rigorous
imprisonment for a term which may extend to 1 (one) year, or with fine, or with
both, if he, without reasonable cause,—
(a) fails or refuses to furnish information within the time prescribed
under section 200, 201, 204 or 205;
(b) refuses to permit inspection or to allow copies to be taken in
accordance with the provisions of section 202;
(c) fails to comply with the requirement under sub-section (2) of
section 204;
(d) fails to afford necessary facilities or to furnish the required
information to an income tax authority exercising power under
section 205;
(e) refuses to permit or in any manner obstructs the exercise of powers
under section 147 or 206 by an income tax authority;
(f) fails to comply with the order made under sub-section (1) of section
223.
